A||N||20||David Bartlett||Digital Speedometer Circuit - Schematic||||1||
Z||000000||David Bartlett||12-02-2001||12:28 PM||||I've been looking into building my own Digital Speedometer and was wondering if anyone has come across an easy to follow schematics for such a purpose.<P> I found one on the net, but the schematic wasn't labeled, which makes it difficult for a beginner like me. I've also seen Oliver's HUD schematic but after looking into EPROM programming it seems a little complex for me.<P>Sure, I could buy one, but what would I learn from that.<P>Anyone have any of there own designs? Found any online, in books? Or just want to help me out?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||12-02-2001||01:21 PM||||Well......... considering Oliver's price for a pre-programmed PIC, it's worth the money.<P>Maybe we can get him to give us a bulk deal. I'd be interested in one.<P>Where did Oliver move his site to?<P>Terry<BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||David Bartlett||12-02-2001||01:35 PM||||Oliver's got a nice schematic.. easy to follow and easy to build... excluding the controller.<P>My whole thing is to learn how to build it! If I can learn how to display the info the vss is putting out then I can modify that circuit to display DTE.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||David Bartlett||12-02-2001||01:54 PM||||this is a great Fiero-electronics related site. I don't know if hes on the board yet...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/techno.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/techno.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||12-02-2001||02:30 PM||||Well, you have to count VSS pulses over a set period of time. The speedo is nothing but a frequency counter. 1.11Hz/MPH (for 4004 pulses/mile).<P>Set up a timer to interupt the processor. Count incoming pulses over that timer period. Do the math, display the results.<P>Well, you could invert that and count timer pulses over the period between VSS pulses. At some point, you can't go too low on MPH since it will take too long to get two pulses from the VSS. Once you pick your display update rate, that will set your lowest MPH you can display.<P>As you can see, Oliver used a stamp/pic for the circuit.<P>DTE?<P>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-02-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||David Bartlett||12-02-2001||03:19 PM||||Wow! Terry K, have you built a speedo yourself? Sounds like you know alot about electronics. I on the other hand can look at a schematic and pretty much build it... Thats it, I havent had any classes in electronics, but after playing around with some stuff I can usually figure out how to make something.<P>I also realize that what I want to do is count pulses.. I've read something about comparing the pulses to a 555 timer.<P>Terry, can you draw up a schematic for me that I can build the unit from?||||reg||1
Z||000006||David Bartlett||12-02-2001||03:30 PM||||DTE - Distance till Empty||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||12-02-2001||03:55 PM||||Well, the problem is that I'd use a PIC or stamp like Oliver and the schematic would wind up looking like his essentially.<P>For $25, it's just not worth it. I'm looking for some seven segement vacuum displays rather than using the LED's.<P>I have a GTP HUD, but it's too big to mount in the Fiero. I need something smaller and OS's looks like the ticket. No need for inverting or moving mirrors like the GTP HUD.<P><BR>TK||||reg||1
Z||000008||David Bartlett||12-02-2001||04:59 PM||||So your saying that you would also use a eprom micro-controller (with a program like hud)?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||rockcrawl||12-02-2001||06:21 PM||||I built a digital speedometer several years ago. I think I still have it around somewhere. I found the circuit in one of the electronics magazines, I think it was a Dakota Digital design. It had a large 3 digit display and a bargragh. I'll see if I can dig up the old article if you're interested.<P>Jon||||reg||7
Z||000010||rockcrawl||12-02-2001||06:45 PM||||I found the speedo, but not the magazine article. It consists of a display board and a contol board. The conrol board is double sided and was a pita to make. I don't recognize any of the chips except the display drivers and some CMOS logic gates, but there is no microprocessor. It has a crystal oscilator. I'll see if I can find my old magazines.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/digispeedo.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||David Bartlett||12-02-2001||06:45 PM||||rockcrawl your amazing! Thats exactly what I'm looking for! Im so excited!<P>You can email me the info if you find it - kenner@cgocable.net If you can't find the article could you even take a few digital pictures of the one you built?<P>WOW! You've made my day!<P>Dave.||||reg||1
